---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

---

<Base title="About: grclanker">
  <!-- Hero illustration -->
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full">
      <img src="/about-clanker.webp" alt="A clanker robot working at a compliance workstation" class="w-full h-full object-cover object-center" loading="eager" />
    </div>
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-b from-base/30 via-base/60 to-base pointer-events-none"></div>
    <div class="relative z-10 max-w-content mx-auto px-6 pt-24 pb-16 text-center">
      <h1 class="font-bold text-3xl md:text-4xl text-text hero-text-shadow">
        What is grclanker
      </h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-content mx-auto px-6 pb-12">
    <div class="about-intro-grid">
      <div class="about-copy-stack">
        <div class="viewscreen rounded-lg p-6 md:p-8 scanlines relative -mt-8">
          <div class="relative z-10 space-y-5 text-subtext1 leading-relaxed">
            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 justify-center md:justify-start">
              <img src="/badges/audited-by-clanker.webp" alt="Audited by Clanker badge" class="h-24 w-24 rounded-full" loading="lazy" />
              <img src="/badges/spec-driven.webp" alt="Spec Driven badge" class="h-24 w-24 rounded-full" loading="lazy" />
            </div>

            <div class="text-sm text-subtext0 space-y-1.5 font-mono">
              <p>Built by <a href="https://ethantroy.dev">Ethan Troy</a></p>
              <p><a href="https://ethantroy.dev">ethantroy.dev</a></p>
              <p><a href="https://github.com/ethanolivertroy/grclanker">GitHub</a></p>
            </div>

            <div class="hud-divider !my-7"></div>

            <p>
              <strong class="text-text">grclanker</strong> is an open source compliance agent with 241 domain tools. Its 35 repository integration specs are implemented as native checks, assessments, and evidence exports. CMVP, KEV, EPSS, FedRAMP, Vanta, SCF, and OSCAL tools round out the current surface.
            </p>

            <p>
              The same prompts, personas, and domain tools run in the Pi terminal CLI, the Cursor Agent SDK project, and the Flue Framework adapter. The Pi path supports local-first models or an explicitly configured hosted provider.
            </p>

            <p>
              The project exists because compliance evidence is scattered across vendor dashboards, government feeds, and spreadsheets. grclanker gathers that evidence, maps it to controls, and packages the result for review.
            </p>

            <p>
              Shared hardening scrubs credential-shaped error text, marks incomplete collections, reports pagination stops, and avoids overwriting prior exports. Runtime adapters validate tool schemas, classify read effects, and put approval gates around writer tools where the host supports them.
            </p>

            <p>
              Every raw spec remains an agent-agnostic build plan with APIs, authentication, control mappings, architecture, and test guidance. Browse them at <a href="/specs" class="text-blue hover:underline">/specs</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="about-robot-column" aria-label="grclanker field unit">
        <div class="about-robot-card">
          <div class="about-robot-meta">
            <span class="hud-label">Field Unit</span>
            <span class="about-robot-status"><span class="led led-live"></span> Local-first CLI</span>
          </div>
          <div class="about-robot-figure">
            <img
              src="/about/grclanker-robot-v1-transparent.png"
              alt="Full-body illustration of the grclanker robot"
              class="about-robot-image"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <section class="page-image-break mt-8" aria-label="About ambient frame">
      <img
        src="/footer/standby.webp"
        alt=""
        class="page-image-break-image"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <div class="page-image-break-overlay">
        <span class="page-image-break-pill">Open source // local-first // experimental by design</span>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
